    <section class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Editing Zhex</p>
      <h1>Syntax highlighting,<br>editor by editor.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Local packages bring Zhex highlighting to Vim and Neovim, VS Code, and Zed.</p>
      <p class="aside">Themes choose the colors. The packages recognize keywords, types, word definitions, calls, numbers, strings, escapes, and comments, with four-space indentation and <code>#</code> comments built in.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="vim-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">01 · Vim and Neovim</p><h2 id="vim-title">Standard Vim syntax.</h2></div>
        <p class="intro">The package uses Vim's native syntax files, so no Tree-sitter installation is needed. It sets buffer-local spacing and comment options, with an undo command for those options.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="command-block"><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/desireco/zhex.git
cd zhex
just vim-install</code></pre></div>
      <p class="access-note">The installer links this checkout into <code>~/.vim/pack/zhex/start/zhex</code> and <code>~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/zhex/start/zhex</code>. Keep the checkout at its current path; repeating the command is safe. Restart, open a <code>.zhex</code> file, and <code>:set filetype?</code> should report <code>zhex</code>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="vscode-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">02 · VS Code</p><h2 id="vscode-title">TextMate highlighting.</h2></div>
        <p class="intro">The extension adds TextMate highlighting, <code>#</code> comments, parentheses and quote pairing, and indentation rules. Build it locally with a current Node.js LTS release and npm.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="command-block"><pre><code>cd editors/vscode
npm ci
npm test
npm run package
code --install-extension ../../dist/editors/zhex-0.0.1.vsix</code></pre></div>
      <p class="access-note">You can also run <strong>Extensions: Install from VSIX</strong> and select the built file. Open a <code>.zhex</code> file and confirm the language mode is <strong>Zhex</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="zed-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">03 · Zed</p><h2 id="zed-title">Tree-sitter grammar.</h2></div>
        <p class="intro">The Zed extension uses the repository's Tree-sitter grammar and adds bracket matching and a word-definition outline. Prepare a dev-extension folder, then install it from disk.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="command-block"><pre><code>just zed-prepare
# Zed → Extensions → Install Dev Extension → select dist/editors/zed</code></pre></div>
      <p class="access-note">The command needs Go 1.23 or newer and Git, writes only generated files under <code>dist/</code>, and prints the folder to select. Zed builds the grammar and recognizes <code>.zhex</code> files as <strong>Zhex</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="example-notes">
      <p class="eyebrow">Worth knowing</p>
      <h2>Where editors stop.</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Editors highlight statements line by line; the interpreter remains responsible for validating indentation, scope, and types.</li>
        <li>Themes choose the highlighting colors; the packages provide the structure.</li>
        <li>The packages are local for now. Extension-store publication, language-server completion, live compiler diagnostics, and formatting are future work.</li>
      </ul>
